      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SKEDADDLE ELLA (1) wasn't far away at the finish when 4th and beaten only 2.5 lengths (21.28) at this track. Safe beginner who draws ideally on the inside. Has winning claims on her best figures. HOPE FOR MOLLY (8) has an honest record despite remaining a maiden and overdue for a win, having placed six of 21 career runs. Should be about the money. ZIPPING DAWSON (5) jumped from a middle draw last time and could manage only fifth and beaten 3.5 lengths (21.33) at this track. Worth following up. OPO STAR (4) is a Clifford Bell-trained newcomer by Bernardo out of Hardship. No favours with the draw and will need to begin well. Profiles nicely and can feature in the finish.",
